Read dconf in-process instead of running the dconf tool (needs 0003, 0009).

0003 (device pixel ratio) and 0009 (display cut-outs) read Lipstick's and
Silica's settings with popen("dconf read ..."). Sandboxed apps (Sailjail)
have no shell or dconf tool, since /usr/bin in the sandbox holds only the
app's own binary. The reads then failed silently: no cut-outs, and the pixel
ratio fell back to the wl_output size (2.5 instead of 2.25 on the Jolla
Phone 2026).

They now use libdconf (dconf_client_read) and g_variant_print, which gives
the same text the dconf tool prints, so the parsing is unchanged. Sailjail's
base permission already allows the dconf files. Needs dconf-devel to build;
libdconf.so.1 is on every Sailfish OS device.

